+              <dd pn="section-5.1-5.6.2.8">Speak</dd>
+              <dt pn="section-5.1-5.6.2.9">8</dt>
+              <dd pn="section-5.1-5.6.2.10">Standby</dd>
+              <dt pn="section-5.1-5.6.2.11">16</dt>
+              <dd pn="section-5.1-5.6.2.12">Active</dd>
+            </dl>
+          </dd>
+          <dt pn="section-5.1-5.7">Hellotime:  1 octet</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-5.1-5.8">
+            <t indent="0" pn="section-5.1-5.8.1">This field is only meaningful in Hello messages.  It contains the
+approximate period between the Hello messages that the router
+sends.  The time is given in seconds.</t>
+            <t indent="0" pn="section-5.1-5.8.2">If the Hellotime is not configured on a router, then it <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> be
